Z||000000||fieroburton||07-27-2001||05:46 PM||||today I was teaching myself to drive a stick and was doing well when I staled the car I started her up and tried again , and I was doing good then I staled again but this time car did not start ! I checked the battery and its good and all my lights work and radio! is it my starter ? and if it is were can I get a new one and for how much ?<BR>its a old 84 SE and always ran good .<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||mrgone||07-27-2001||06:20 PM||||check the wires going to the starter, especially the one comin from the battery. if they are loose or rusty its an easy fix.<P>and you know since you have stick you can bumpstart it by getting the car rolling down a hill (about 10kmph) and letting out the clutch in 1st (tap gas i think correct me if wrong. floor gas if stranded)<P>my bettery died at 3am in a mall parking lot||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||07-27-2001||06:43 PM||||Might try bypassing the clutch safety switch (the one that keeps you from cranking it while in gear w/o clutch).  It's located at top of clutch pedal - has at least one heavy purple wire going to it.<P>Rebuilt starter shouldn't exceed $50 (a long time ago, anyway); installation isn't the most fun, though. <P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroburton||07-27-2001||09:21 PM||||ok I checked all the wires and pushed them in<BR>I tried to start it and it didn't work so I left it alone,just now I went outside and tried to start it and now it works so I'm confused but not as worried  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>thanks a lot for the tips and I dint know about the button above the clutch ,thanks a lot! <BR>(i love this forum )<P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||fieroburton||07-27-2001||10:43 PM||||I just started my car to but it in the back yard and it was running good . then the lights started to dim and the radio started to distort to the point I could not hear the music just static and thumping and I think the rpm's went down too . so now im thinking its the battery , but what do you all think ? <BR>the volt meter is always at 11 is that good ?<BR>this will be the last time I buy a autozone brand battery &gt; <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>1984 2M4 SE <BR>    <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fieroburton/1.html</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000005||Jim Jimenez||07-27-2001||11:55 PM||||Sounds as if you have a severe low voltage problem with the alternator or the wiring to it. Voltage should read 15-18 volts with the engine running, and 12-12.5 with the engine off. ||||reg||10
Z||000006||starfighter007@msn.com||07-28-2001||04:44 PM||||yes I would agree you have a alternator problem for starters no pun intended.your alternater should put out at least 12 volts min.any thing less you will get stranded somewhere.after you get alternator changed I believe you still have a starter problem that you have to deal with.I am guessing all that start and stopping teaching yourself to drive stick has taken its toll on the starter.they cant take a lot of heat and a lot of cranking with out haveing time to cool down enough. let us know when you are ready to tackle these problems we are here to help you out in any way we can.||||reg||1
